From 476d2d9dc3f848ac2d85e987ef25f15b9fb07bc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wmehanna <wassimmehanna@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:43:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] perf(tcg): cut BQL use, add a return stack and a branch site
 cache

Hot paths of the AArch64 TCG front end for a long running macOS guest.

- Read the generic timer counters, clear EXITTB, skip masked
  interrupts and call EL change hooks without the BQL.
- Sync guest state only on the slow path of loads and stores.
- Generate the vmapple compat PAC inline.
- Per-vCPU return address stack, a branch site cache for BR, BLR and
  direct branches to another page, validated by the code TLB.
- Zero DC ZVA blocks with stores, fence a release store only where an
  acquire load follows (P26_FENCE=0 restores the old mapping), publish
  the branch site cache with release.
- Counters behind P35_STATS and an opt-in indirect exit count.
- System tests: stlr-ldar with two vCPUs, PAC strip across TCR_EL1 and
  EL changes, bti-guarded.
